1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:04,150
This portfolio covers three decisions in defensive security.

2
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:13,965
The examples use simulated Windows events, dependency reports, and wireless observations. One component check ran on real installed software.

3
00:00:14,525 --> 00:00:19,515
The Windows rule groups sign-ins by account, host, source, and logon type.

4
00:00:19,775 --> 00:00:29,290
At five failures, one case was missed by a single second. Four failures surfaced both review cases. At two, the rule also flagged a confirmed typing error.

5
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:38,810
In the dependency review, one advisory changed its identifier, and one package was skipped. Neither observation justified closing the issue.

6
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:47,140
A separate reference template passed three rendering checks on a local Jinja installation. The original chatbot was outside this test.

7
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:54,540
In the wireless case, the change record approved one new radio. That reduced flagged observations from three to two.

8
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:00,855
A known radio still reported an unexpected security mode. Two incomplete readings needed fresh evidence.

9
00:01:01,415 --> 00:01:06,160
The casebook and source archive include the inputs, outputs, and decision notes.

10
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:11,785
The offline replay and nineteen passing regression tests make the results reproducible.

